Q16. Count the total number of students in the Student table
SELECT COUNT(*) AS Total_Students
FROM Student;


COUNT(*) counts all rows in the Student table.

Q17. Create a table with a primary key constraint
CREATE TABLE Department (
    DeptId   NUMBER(3) PRIMARY KEY,
    DeptName VARCHAR2(50)
);


 DeptId is Primary Key → ensures uniqueness + NOT NULL.

Q18. Create a table with all columns having NOT NULL constraints
CREATE TABLE Faculty (
    FacultyId   NUMBER(3) NOT NULL,
    FacultyName VARCHAR2(50) NOT NULL,
    Subject     VARCHAR2(30) NOT NULL
);


Every column must have a value (no NULL allowed).

Q19. Create a foreign key constraint referencing the Course table
CREATE TABLE Enrollment (
    EnrollId   NUMBER(3) PRIMARY KEY,
    StudentId  NUMBER(4),
    CourseId   NUMBER(2),
    CONSTRAINT fk_course FOREIGN KEY (CourseId) REFERENCES Course(CourseID)
);


CourseId in Enrollment references CourseID in Course.

Q20. Create a table with a UNIQUE key constraint on a column
CREATE TABLE Library (
    BookId     NUMBER(4) PRIMARY KEY,
    ISBN       VARCHAR2(20) UNIQUE,
    Title      VARCHAR2(100)
);


ISBN must be unique, but can accept NULL (unlike primary key).
 Q21. Display different students from departments 1 and 2

(Join Student–Course tables, filter by DeptNo)

SELECT DISTINCT s.StudentName, c.DeptNo
FROM Student s
JOIN Course c ON s.Course = c.Dname
WHERE c.DeptNo IN (1, 2);


 DISTINCT ensures unique student names.

 Q22. Display the list of students ordered by course
